#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4386227a-d159-5ea7-b586-57eb8ba8b3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309258} {:answer/id #uuid "ce0f7ff2-63f3-536e-a712-0b2b5f23cf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin(5t)+\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce0f7ff2-63f3-536e-a712-0b2b5f23cf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin(5t)+\\cos(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506276} :answer-field/id #uuid "53651861-1195-570e-a314-53031aadafea" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17eab3e0-25a6-5d97-ab26-3bfb684afa0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308938} {:answer/id #uuid "2633b2d1-98e4-54f9-bd3d-9d6754122e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505974}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2633b2d1-98e4-54f9-bd3d-9d6754122e46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos(5t)+\\sin(5t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505974} :answer-field/id #uuid "d170c52a-07fe-5c77-8bee-10ab3fcdbfb2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "622243a2-b3f9-5f58-9668-ac4d025f3264" :question/math-academy-id "q-335260" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\, \\\\ \\,3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311560 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95d4b157-bf69-5bf7-9aad-3eba516db410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{cos}(7t)-3\\operatorname{sin}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309947} {:answer/id #uuid "979f156d-01a6-59f8-8aca-1c984d058959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos(7t)-3\\sin(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "979f156d-01a6-59f8-8aca-1c984d058959" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos(7t)-3\\sin(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186506174} :answer-field/id #uuid "334b3886-7b34-5ba0-9e2a-91b524ea209a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310929} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "edb27977-979e-5d5d-9ca0-7fdf66c63c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}(7t)+3\\operatorname{cos}(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310639} {:answer/id #uuid "2678d709-b8ee-55e1-bb84-a652beb39148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin(7t)+3\\cos(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2678d709-b8ee-55e1-bb84-a652beb39148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin(7t)+3\\cos(7t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186505975} :answer-field/id #uuid "89b7d71a-ace4-5436-8715-dcb69e35eeb8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "085673d9-6167-5c0c-b43c-bc1e085569fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-335262" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"170px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)\\, \\\\ \\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t)+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77290e62-6148-5a0c-a377-bec8579eec5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309679} {:answer/id #uuid "97fc3697-404e-5fb0-854e-fc0c8ff7d45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2t{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309968} {:answer/id #uuid "9a02425e-0f01-5418-94f2-288ad58f1b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309988} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c51a8a-3c2a-5bdb-a554-d4a1fb8e8ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ -2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310100} {:answer/id #uuid "d266e8d7-9b0b-5943-9acc-ac02de0e98d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d266e8d7-9b0b-5943-9acc-ac02de0e98d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310440} :answer-field/id #uuid "a01f0c87-7802-5bf3-a753-2547be1ae761" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "62010a37-a91d-55bc-8c8e-6361d12d6c44" :question/math-academy-id "q-335267" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-3t} & t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2t{e}^{-3t} \\\\ 2{e}^{-3t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "942a629e-94b8-5c24-bbcc-97e7d789cb40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391588} {:answer/id #uuid "9b04c091-3bbb-5dae-9ed9-1a467ab29d95" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391589} {:answer/id #uuid "07f2c784-653a-5833-9229-3fb331cf19a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391590} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea30351-9279-59bc-8f85-f17f0652612d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391591} {:answer/id #uuid "150d70c1-d912-530b-b05b-4c87bea0ff00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "150d70c1-d912-530b-b05b-4c87bea0ff00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391592} :answer-field/id #uuid "36126579-e63c-590b-a6f7-f58bde2b64a5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6580aa1b-3c6f-5533-9e32-e7afb350be95" :question/math-academy-id "q-335450" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-3x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-(-1))}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1)) & -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3(t+1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3(t+1))\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311794 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17966dd8-73ff-5dae-a604-448905e652ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308934} {:answer/id #uuid "6427f8ed-49bc-5e1b-ad8d-b32b63aa2584" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "by substitution from line $\\text{L2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309517} {:answer/id #uuid "fc75620b-35c9-591c-aade-7daa879c2824" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the fact that ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310766}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17966dd8-73ff-5dae-a604-448905e652ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "by substituting $t={t}_{0}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308934} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f5ad037-aae6-5cab-bcba-d870b9717a79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310836} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3586d768-5a6b-55e3-b74b-d7384ddf8b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309155} {:answer/id #uuid "96845e88-24f3-523a-aa89-8c99b1e81691" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At}$ for any matrix $A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309954} {:answer/id #uuid "9af374b3-6d71-58a8-b886-dbe3e18d9a85" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3586d768-5a6b-55e3-b74b-d7384ddf8b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}$ when $X$ and $Y$ commute" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309155} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7d8c45-9baf-5f3c-9730-e684d4f25418" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b4f6d50-4cc2-5464-88dd-148342d77dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309204} {:answer/id #uuid "757e14df-a5bc-5543-aecf-5b5c92b609a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{A{t}_{0}}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}=I{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309664} {:answer/id #uuid "b7846f39-941e-5fc0-a5af-9df9b5d9178c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={e}^{A{t}_{0}}I" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b4f6d50-4cc2-5464-88dd-148342d77dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309204} :answer-field/id #uuid "e445eb61-c230-53f6-a72a-4588c5fa0f2d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311455}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "45874040-9e7b-5fb5-9a00-ef344d9b3cd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-337109" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x({t}_{0})$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$  \n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$  \n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,c$ \n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ $x({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c$  \n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $c={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L7}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L8}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\n$\\text{L9}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}x({t}_{0})\\,$  \n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$  Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}.$ Starting from $\\text{L3},$\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwe evaluate both sides at $t={t}_{0}$ to obtain\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L4}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L4}$ follows from $\\text{L3}$ $\\text{by substituting }t={t}_{0}.$\n\n- Next, we consider lines $\\text{L5}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Line $\\text{L5}$ gives\n\n$$\n({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0})=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c.\n$$\n\nSince $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}{e}^{A{t}_{0}}={I}_{n}$, the right-hand side simplifies to $c$, so\n\n$$\nc=({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nSimplify once, then apply $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}$, to obtain\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}),\n$$\n\nwhich is line $\\text{L6}.$ Therefore, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L5}$ by the fact that $({e}^{A{t}_{0}})^{-1}={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L7}$ and $\\text{L8}.$ Since $At$ and $-A{t}_{0}$ commute, we can use the property \n\n$$\n{e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into line $\\text{L7},$ we get line $\\text{L8}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{At-A{t}_{0}}x({t}_{0})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{L8}$ follows from $\\text{L7}$ by the fact that ${e}^{X}{e}^{Y}={e}^{X+Y}\\text{ when }X\\text{ and }Y\\text{ commute}.$"}]}
